# Project Proposal and Problem Statement

## Project Title
Development of a Digital Avatar Platform for Advertising Video Production and Campaign Personalization

## Team
- Karina Anvarbekova
- Fariza Ismagambetova

Supervisor: Shyngys Alshynov

## Problem Statement
Advertising video production requires script preparation, recording, editing and content review. Preparing different videos for several audiences or languages can require additional work.

The project investigates whether digital avatars can support regular advertising video production and campaign personalization.

The platform is proposed as a possible solution. Its usefulness and potential time savings still need to be evaluated.

## Target Users
The primary users are public relations staff who prepare announcements and promotional videos.

The secondary users are Media Technologies students who explore creative digital content production.

## Project Aim
To develop and evaluate a digital avatar platform based on user needs and advertising production practices.

## Objectives
1. Analyse existing advertising video production practices.
2. Conduct three to five documented discussions with potential users.
3. Review survey findings and scientific research.
4. Define and prioritise system requirements.
5. Develop a prototype and evaluate its usefulness.

## Research Questions
1. Which production stages require the most effort?
2. When are different versions of advertising messages needed?
3. Which avatar, speech and language characteristics affect video quality?
4. Which features would make the platform useful?

## Preliminary Scope
The project focuses on short promotional videos, editable scripts, avatar selection, campaign versions and human review.

Training new video generation models, building a complete professional video editor and automatic advertising targeting are outside the proposed scope.

## Expected Outcomes
- Clear problem definition
- Documented user needs
- Prioritised requirements
- Prototype design and later implementation
- Evaluation of the proposed workflow

## Current Status
The project proposal and preliminary scope have been documented. Further research and implementation are planned.
